# eoreader6.1 · kernel · turn 015
# Act: CON−  (Connection aimed at Ground)   Stance: Tending   Site: Field
#
# The Structure triad's second operator, first use. SEG "draws a boundary
# or partition" (turn-9, turn-10); CON "creates a relationship between
# entities" (EO Event Streaming §3, Operator Definitions — "corresponds to
# JOIN, foreign key assignment, graph edge creation"). CON− is the move
# before any specific relationship is drawn: recognizing that turn-10's
# partitioned field is one where entities CAN stand in relation to their
# side of the boundary — not yet which entity, which side.
#
# Earning argument: precondition is turn-10 (a partitioned field to relate
# within) and, for there to be anything to relate, at least one anchored
# entity — satisfied twice over, by turn-12 and turn-13. This turn commits
# to nothing about either individually; it only tends to the field as
# relational.

:turn-15  eot:opens        :turn-14 .
:turn-15  eot:act          eot:CON- .
:turn-15  eot:stance       "Tending" .
:turn-15  eot:site         "Field" .
:turn-15  eot:tends        "turn-10's partitioned field, as relational" .
:turn-15  eot:closes       [ eot:aperture 1.0 ; eot:perturbation "none" ] .
